lly considered weak because the board edges limit the number of directions in which lines of five can be formed (fewer diagonals and restricted horizontal/vertical expansion). Because the center of the board is completely open, the most strategic response is to claim the center point. This allows White to exert maximum influence over the board and sets up lines of attack in all directions.\n\nReason: With the opponent playing passively in the corner, taking the center square (H8) is the optimal strategy. It maximizes potential connections and board control, effectively giving White the advantage of the "first move" in the main playing area. There are no immediate threats to block.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "H", "row": 8}'}
